  "ERRATUM_2026-08-10": {
    "what": "the key arms.*.verdict.M4_no_conditioning is WRONG and must not be used",
    "why": "it was computed from |gt - antonym|, but the antonym context flips only colour-direction words (darker<->brighter) and leaves the subject phrase intact. q3vl/whereb/antonyms.py and metrics.py:282 antonym_invariance make invariance the PASS condition (pre-registered |delta| <= 0.05, explicitly 'a negative-control column, not a gate'). W01's published board reports antonym_invariance.median_abs_delta = 0.0, within_threshold = true.",
    "corrected_reading": "M4 is NOT supported. The correct conditioning probes are the subject-swapping ones: on W01's board the gt median grid_soft_iou is 0.550 vs shuffled 0.405 (-0.145), fixed_phrase 0.320 (-0.230), irrelevant_words 0.312 (-0.238). The instruction does condition the output; it just buys only +0.033 over the zero-parameter centre prior (0.517). That is M3, not M4.",
    "unaffected": [
      "i_constant_output",
      "ii_what_explains_it",
      "verdict.M3_copies_geometric_prior (still true, both arms)"
    ]
  }
